% docs/references.bib: the works this repository relies on, one entry each
% (swarm-routing/.github CONTRIBUTING "References"; checked in CI by
% `fidelity.py bib check` once the file has an entry).
%
% Roles, in `keywords`: implemented (the work this repository implements),
% restates, compared, dataset, tool, background. The implemented, tool and
% dataset entries are rendered into CITATION.cff `references:` and the README's
% "Releases & citing" section by org-sync: edit them here, never there. The
% README follows on the next `org_sync.py apply`; CITATION.cff is a seed, so
% refresh it with `org_sync.py reseed CITATION.cff` and review the diff.
%
% Every entry gives its DOI; a url only for a work that has none. Never this
% repository's own DOI: CITATION.cff carries it. Public sources only: a work is
% cited by its DOI link, never by where a copy of it is kept.
%
% Never type an entry or a field: take it from Crossref or Zenodo,
%   python3 -I tools/fidelity/fidelity.py bib entry DOI --key K --role R
%   python3 -I tools/zenodo/zenodo.py bibtex OWNER/REPO --key K --role tool
% (both in swarm-routing/.github). A work with no DOI (a thesis, a report)
% takes its fields from its publisher's or institution's record, with its url
% and no doi. With nothing to cite yet, the file stays
% this header alone.
